{
 "schema": "headroom.circuit.v1",
 "id": "test-dc-microsynth",
 "minRate": 176400,
 "version": 1,
 "name": "DC regression: EHX Micro Synthesizer (snapshot of the wave-e WIP netlist, ENGINE_QUEUE item 32)",
 "description": "Frozen snapshot of work/circuit-netlists/wave-e/ehx-micro-synth-76000.wip.json as of the ENGINE_QUEUE item 32 report (2026-11-10), kept as the SPICE-export regression: its nodes \"nC2\" (VCF input RC) and \"nc2\" (the CD4013 latch Q) differ only in case, which plain SPICE folds into one node, shorting the filter onto the flip-flop; and its five CA3094 OTAs, whose output halves now mirror the abc diode current through a sense source. The engine DC is compared with ngspice .op on every node. Original description: 1978 EHX Guitar Micro Synthesizer: RC4558 preamp/700 Hz LPF, full-wave rectifier, smoothing+log envelope, trigger/stop/attack detectors, CA3094 square-wave voice, CD4013 trigger latch + divide-by-two, CA3094 sub-octave track-and-hold, 3-pole CA3094 ladder filter with resonance and CA3094 sweep, CA3094 VCA with attack-delay.",
 "sources": [
  {
   "title": "Electro-Harmonix GUITAR MICRO SYNTHESIZER schematic, 3 sheets (D. Cockerell rev 12/12/78, drawn F.P. Hartery 1996)",
   "url": "https://github.com/yuvadm/guitar-effects-schematics/blob/master/Guitar%20Synth%20and%20Misc%20Signal%20Shapers/Electro%20Harmonix%20Micro%20Synthesizer.pdf"
  },
  {
   "title": "EHX XO Micro Synthesizer manual (control set and behaviour)",
   "url": "https://www.ehx.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/micro-synth-manual.pdf"
  }
 ],
